# large artifacts stay out of git (obtune convention): manifests, resolved configs and
# run_manifest.json files ARE committed; adapters, corpora, trials and caches are not.
data/
# runs/ is entirely generated. The sbatch scripts are provenance ONLY for jobs that really
# ran, and `--dry-run` writes one too — committing those would be a record of runs that never
# happened. Real provenance lives in each adapter's run_manifest.json and each result's
# summary.json, which carry the git sha, the resolved config and the script hashes.
runs/
results/
third_party/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.log

# papers/ IS committed: the literature this project positions against is part of the record,
# and a related-work claim that cannot be checked against the actual PDF is not a claim.
!papers/
!papers/*.pdf
